 "version": 1,
 "name": "SSL 4000 G quad bus compressor (82E26 x4 + 82E27)",
 "description": "The SL651G master module's compressor as drawn on T82026.71.3 rev 6A (82E26 '651G QUAD BUS MIX AMPS + COMPRESSOR') and T82027.71.3 rev 4A (82E27 'COMPRESSOR, QUAD FADER/AUTO FADER'). Each bus card carries an audio dbx 202X (A1) and a side-chain 202X (A2) fed the same control plus the threshold offset; the side-chain VCA's output is full-wave rectified (T6/T7), shaped by the ratio network in T7's feedback, and diode-OR'd onto bus D (D6). 82E27 charges the selected release capacitor from D through the attack resistor, buffers it (T1) and sums it into line B (audio VCAs, with make-up) and line C (side-chain VCAs, with threshold). Left and right are the bus A and B cards in full; the quad C/D cards carry no signal and appear as their four 202X control ports on lines B and C. The netlist starts at the PRE COMP RETURN (the mix amplifier ahead of it is the bus summer) and ends at the card OUTPUT (pin 28) with the pre/post patch points normalled.",
 "sources": [
  {
   "title": "Solid State Logic SL4000G Console Service Manual v1.1, PDF p.204: T82026.71.3 '651G QUAD BUS MIX AMPS + COMPRESSOR' rev 6A (21 Sep 92) - source of record for 82E26",
   "url": "https://funkwerkes.com/web/wp-content/techdocs/MixedProAudio/SSL-4000G-Console-Service-Manual-v1_1.pdf"
  },
  {
   "title": "Same manual, PDF p.206: T82027.71.3 'COMPRESSOR, QUAD FADER/AUTO FADER' rev 4A (26 Oct 92) - source of record for 82E27; pp.202/205 the edge-connector lists (A/B/C/D, ratio 37/38/39 = 10/4/2, attack 43-48, release 5-9)",
   "url": "https://funkwerkes.com/web/wp-content/techdocs/MixedProAudio/SSL-4000G-Console-Service-Manual-v1_1.pdf"
  },
  {
   "title": "K&A Electronics: SSL 82E26 (T82026.71 rev 8, 3.8.84 redrawn) and 82E27 (T82027.71 rev 8, Dec 85) - the E-series cards, cross-check of every side-chain and time-constant value",
   "url": "http://www.ka-electronics.com/images/SSL/ssl_82E26.pdf"
  },
  {
   "title": "gyraf: SSL 82E26 / 82E27 hand drawings (rev 6, E) and 'The SSL Mixbus Compressor Clone' (meter law ~50 uA/dB, threshold end marks +-15 dB, the 202XT's internal control buffer)",
   "url": "https://gyraf.dk/gy_pd/ssl/ssl.html"
